      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree, a winding set of stairs stretched downward into the gloom. Perched upon the very top step sat an old, grey fox wearing a tattered green vest. This was Mosk, the guardian of the tree. His voice rustled like dry leaves as he warned Lina that this place was not for visitors, urging her to turn back and forget the humming sound. But Lina shook her head, insisting that she could not forget a melody she had not yet truly heard."
