{
  "bridge_text": "The firefly's faint light pulses like a heartbeat in the dim room, and Mosk watches her with such hopeful eyes. The truth of her fate rests in the quiet melody beginning to fill the air.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "The poor firefly's glow was flickering, nearly spent. Mosk's whiskers trembled as he looked at her; he remembered that long-ago winter when he had arrived too late with his medicine. He had guarded this tree ever since, carrying the heavy weight of his shame, never daring to hope he might make things right after all these years."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt softly and asked the firefly queen what she needed to feel strong again. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, the queen whispered, explaining that was all the medicine she had ever truly required. Mosk hurried to fetch the milk in a tiny thimble, laying his paw gently beside hers. As she drank, the queen's glow steadied, and the tree's humming blossomed into a new, hopeful tune that Mosk finally hummed along with."
    }
